159	<section>
160	  <h2>Every run we did <span class="eyebrow">scored on the same 5,000 test trips</span></h2>
161	  <div class="explain">
162	    <p><b>How to read the numbers.</b> Both scores are in minutes and <b>lower is better</b>. <b>Median error</b>: how far the model's single best guess was from the real delay, on average. <b>CRPS</b>: how good the whole predicted range was; it rewards putting probability where the truth landed and punishes ranges that are too wide or off-centre. "Val" is the May data we used for tuning; "Test" is June to August, which no model saw during training. The differences between rows look small because most trains are nearly on time; the hard cases are where models differ.</p>
163	    <p><b>A "run"</b> is one training of the model with one set of choices. <b>Steps</b> are training iterations; more steps means the model saw more examples. An <b>ablation</b> is an experiment that changes exactly one ingredient to find out whether that ingredient matters.</p>
164	  </div>
